arc-plc/washington/clark-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, July to August came in under 90% of normal in 40 of the 75 years since 1951, the most of any pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 37% of normal in June to July and 52% in April to May. So far in 2026, May to June sits at 64% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 30629 had its driest year in 1985 at 62% of normal.</p>"}
